※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4429 LANG_COLLECTION_KEY_NOT_HASHABLE

※ A key is hashed to find where it might be and then compared to see whether
※ it is there, so a type that can be one is a type `=` answers exactly.
※ Floating point answers none of the three: two values standing for one number
※ may be two values, a not-a-number is equal to nothing including itself, and
※ the two zeroes are equal and hash differently.

let bad: ⸨f64⸩ = ⸨1f64⸩

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    0u8
